ok - fm-spawn.sh --backend t3code: leases the slot, launches the thread on it, records metadata, sends the launch brief
ok - fm-spawn.sh --backend t3code codex: writes .codex/config.toml with GOTMPDIR, FM_TASK_ID, and TRACEPARENT
ok - fm-spawn.sh --backend t3code --secondmate: project on the home, root-strategy thread, charter message, launch prefix as settings env
ok - fm-spawn.sh --backend t3code --secondmate codex: launch prefix as .codex/config.toml shell_environment_policy
